Subject: [PATCH] playlist: append an add-on group in one checked transaction

Use a database transaction and revision tokens for all playlist writers.
Check the complete appended group before commit. Roll back skipped inserts,
changed order, counters, and tokens on error.

Keep snapshots independent of the library lifetime. Test reset and restore,
writer races, schema changes, and existing playlist behavior. Retain exact
lookup of the declared opaque add-on source references. Create a new source
record and its first title in one transaction. Preserve existing titles.

---
diff --git a/include/medialibrary/AddonPlaylist.h b/include/medialibrary/AddonPlaylist.h
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/medialibrary/AddonPlaylist.h
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
+#pragma once
+#include <array>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <vector>
+#include <string>
+
+#define MEDIALIBRARY_HAS_PLAYLIST_CAS 1
+
+namespace medialibrary {
+class IMediaLibrary;
+
+// This value holds no library or database reference.
+struct AddonPlaylistSnapshot {
+    int64_t playlistId = 0;
+    std::array<char, 64> owner{};
+    std::array<char, 64> token{};
+};
+
+// Calls need an active library and no caller-owned database context.
+// A snapshot belongs to one library instance. A reset prevents use of old tokens.
+bool createAddonPlaylistSnapshot(IMediaLibrary&, int64_t playlistId,
+                                AddonPlaylistSnapshot&) noexcept;
+// Append one group of at most 1,000 positive media IDs. A failed append leaves
+// the playlist unchanged. Schema repair can prevent use of old snapshots.
+bool appendAddonPlaylistIfUnchanged(IMediaLibrary&, const AddonPlaylistSnapshot&,
+                                   const std::vector<int64_t>& mediaIds) noexcept;
+// Reuse the exact source record, or create it with its first display title.
+// Existing records retain their title. A failure creates no record.
+bool prepareAddonSourceMedia(IMediaLibrary&, const std::string& canonicalSourceUri,
+                            const std::string& title, int64_t& id) noexcept;
+}
